INT. LUNAR LAVA TUBE - GREENHOUSE - ARTIFICIAL DAY

A cathedral of black basalt, strung with grow-lamps. Rows of tomatoes and soybeans climb trellises under a violet glow. Condensation drips from a vaulted ceiling.

DR. PALOMA REYNOSO, 40s, in a canvas apron over a thermal suit, prunes a tomato vine with delicate care. Behind her, an airlock hisses.

A figure in a worn pressure suit steps through, visor fogged. It stops three paces inside and stands very still, as if afraid to wake the plants.

PALOMA
You're not on the roster.

THE VISITOR
No. I came on the supply drone.

PALOMA
The drone carries cargo.

THE VISITOR
I was cargo.

Paloma sets down her shears. She approaches, slowly, until she can see through the visor to the face behind it: gaunt, unshaven, eyes red.

PALOMA
Take off your helmet.

THE VISITOR
I'd rather not.

PALOMA
Then you can't stay.

He lifts his hands to the seals. The helmet rotates with a hiss. He draws a breath of the humid air and closes his eyes. The scent of tomatoes fills the cave.

PALOMA (CONT'D)
Who are you?

THE VISITOR
Orin Feld. Systems tech, Tycho Base. I left four years ago.

Paloma staggers back against a trellis. The tomatoes sway.

PALOMA
Orin Feld died on the surface. We held a service.

ORIN
I know. I was there. In the back.

PALOMA
You were dead.

ORIN
For a while. It was easier.

Paloma slaps him. The crack echoes off the basalt. Orin does not lift a hand. He just stands, helmet under one arm, cheek reddening.

PALOMA
Four years. Four years, Orin.

ORIN
Paloma--

PALOMA
Dr. Reynoso, to you.

She turns away, shoulders shaking, and presses her palm to a vine. A tomato drops into her hand. She stares at it.

ORIN
It's the first one, isn't it?

PALOMA
The first red one. Yes.

ORIN
Eat it.

She does not move. He steps forward, takes it gently from her fingers, and bites into it. Juice runs down his chin. He laughs. He is crying.

ORIN (CONT'D)
God. I forgot.

Paloma looks at him. Slowly, she smiles, and reaches for another.
